From: Julien Etienne <julien.etienne@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 18:12:50 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] power: supply: mt6351-fuel-gauge: keep the headroom safe
 until the resistance is known

The headroom in current_max uses the learned resistance. Until it is
learned, or restored by userspace, that is the DT's new-cell value, and
on an aged Gemini cell, measured at 0.3-0.4 Ohm against 165 mOhm, the
headroom then reads about twice what the battery can supply. A CPU limit
following it would allow a load the cell cannot hold.

Until the resistance has been learned or written since probe, assume an
aged cell at up to three times the new-cell value at the battery's
temperature, so the headroom does not overstate what any cell can
supply. The learned or restored value replaces it.
---
 drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c | 16 +++++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 15 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
index 002a4ef..6e50c2b 100644
--- a/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
+++ b/drivers/power/supply/mt6351-fuel-gauge.c
@@ -162,6 +162,12 @@
  */
 #define MT6351_FG_HEADROOM_UV		3100000
 #define MT6351_FG_HEADROOM_BAND_UA	100000
+/*
+ * Until the resistance has been learned or restored, the headroom assumes an
+ * aged cell, at up to this many times the DT's new-cell value, so that it
+ * never overstates what the battery can supply.
+ */
+#define MT6351_FG_R_UNKNOWN_FACTOR	3
 
 /*
  * The resistance against 25 C, per mille, every 5 C from -10 to 50 C: the
@@ -203,6 +209,8 @@ struct mt6351_fg {
 	bool rl_done;
 	ktime_t r_time;
 	bool r_updated;
+	/* The resistance was learned or restored since probe. */
+	bool r_known;
 	/* The previous window's current and closing voltage, for the step estimate. */
 	int win_prev_ua;
 	int win_prev_uv;
@@ -436,6 +444,9 @@ static void mt6351_fg_headroom(struct mt6351_fg *fg)
 		return;
 
 	r = max_t(s64, mt6351_fg_r_uohm(fg, mc), 1);
+	if (!fg->r_known)
+		r = max(r, div_s64(r * MT6351_FG_R_UNKNOWN_FACTOR * fg->r_design_uohm,
+				   fg->r25_uohm));
 	fg->headroom_ua = clamp_t(s64, div64_s64((s64)(ocv - MT6351_FG_HEADROOM_UV) * 1000000, r),
 				  0, INT_MAX);
 	band = fg->headroom_ua / MT6351_FG_HEADROOM_BAND_UA;
@@ -696,6 +707,7 @@ static bool mt6351_fg_learn_r(struct mt6351_fg *fg, ktime_t now, int ua, s64 ful
 	fg->r25_uohm += step;
 	fg->r_time = now;
 	fg->r_updated = true;
+	fg->r_known = true;
 	dev_info(fg->dev, "resistance %lld uOhm at 25 C\n", fg->r25_uohm);
 
 	return step != 0;
@@ -1071,8 +1083,10 @@ static ssize_t learned_resistance_uohm_store(struct device *dev,
 	if (!READ_ONCE(fg->info))
 		return -ENODATA;
 
-	scoped_guard(mutex, &fg->lock)
+	scoped_guard(mutex, &fg->lock) {
 		fg->r25_uohm = r;
+		fg->r_known = true;
+	}
 	power_supply_changed(fg->psy);
 
 	return count;
